Experimental testing has been completely re-conducted more extensively with the latest version of GoIntellect (GI) on all three Go categories of 19 × 19, 13 × 13, and 9 × 9 boards. The results show that dynamic randomization increases the playing strength of GI significantly with 128K simulations per move, the improvement is about seven percentage points in the winning rate against GnuGo on 19 × 19 Go over the version of GI without dynamic randomization, about three percentage points on 13 × 13 Go, and four percentage points on 9 × 9 Go.

